On 10/16/26 23:18, Daniel Henrique Barboza wrote:
> Hi,
> 
> Not sure if this belongs to the changes made in these patches but can
> we establish some "rules of engagement" in the mailing list
> discussions w.r.t AI usage in replies?  I know that patch 3 touches
> on it a little bit but I'm talking mostly about mailing list email.

This is currently handled in both the policy and AGENTS.md.  Cover
letters, commit messages, responses to reviewer comments must be written
by people.

> we have cases where the 
> developer keeps sending the same stuff over and over again, and we're
> now wondering whether someone is being cheeky and ignoring feedback
> or if the developer didn't fully understand the feedback, and I bet
> it's the latter.
> 
> I'll assume that we don't want to forbid AI usage in ML replies (might
> as well just forbid AI altogether in that case)

No, that's exactly what we want.  There must be a clear boundary where 
we say "from this point on, you must be participating on your own".  For 
commit messages it may be okay to start with a draft provided by the 
LLM, but in-thread replies done with AI are both disrespectful and a 
waste of time.

Paolo


